                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d29848e8-332e-3b12-8a9a-4e4917abc8e9",
                        "entry_id": "54faafba-a1ba-3999-9f2c-e3b03e7da413",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To deprive of a sceptre; to deprive of the status of monarch or of authority."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef6a35dd-e0c5-45e9-a816-22f5eed38cd2",
                                "sense_id": "d29848e8-332e-3b12-8a9a-4e4917abc8e9",
                                "text": "It is the cuſtome for their Kings to inherite, the ſonne alvvayes taking the Kingdome after his fathers death. If there be no ſonne, then the Queene rules; if no Queene, the next to the blood-royall, vvho comes in othervvise, is but counted an uſurping intruder, and if his faire carriage beare him not out the better, they vvill ſoone unſcepter him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78a54c7d-bb9e-4b0c-a1c3-0c89f8bc8f95",
                                "sense_id": "d29848e8-332e-3b12-8a9a-4e4917abc8e9",
                                "text": "Upon the sodden ground / His [the god Saturn’s] old right hand lay nerveless, listless, dead, / Unsceptred; and his realmless eyes were closed; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55f18404-7c6f-47d5-ab79-ef2c7be0e8f2",
                                "sense_id": "d29848e8-332e-3b12-8a9a-4e4917abc8e9",
                                "text": "Ye hate, shall hatred then unsceptre Zeus, / Or anger empty any throne in heaven?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fafe4293-aa2e-4143-9d15-cdd9f76220c4",
                                "sense_id": "d29848e8-332e-3b12-8a9a-4e4917abc8e9",
                                "text": "I can make kings and unsceptre them, / Yet cannot give my heart to whom I choose."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
